*  earn0_stored_varref.sno - EARN-0 hand-check fallout (2026-08-11 s27).
*  A stored composite pattern that REFERENCES ANOTHER PATTERN-VALUED VARIABLE.
*  Manual p.122: pattern construction is BY VALUE -- only `*` defers -- so P inside Q
*  is fully known at build time and carries NEITHER EARN hazard (not OPAQUE, not
*  UNBOUNDED). EARN's law therefore predicts ZERO frames anywhere in this program.
*  AT HEAD fc5b0754 THIS PRINTS NOTHING AT ALL AND EXITS 0 (silent-empty class).
*  The SAME pattern written inline in the match statement is correct -- see
*  earn0_inline_control.sno. The discriminator is the stored var-reference.
        P = LEN(1)
        Q = POS(0) P LEN(2) RPOS(0)
        'abc' Q                                  :S(Y)F(N)
Y       OUTPUT = 'MATCH'                         :(D)
N       OUTPUT = 'NOMATCH'
D       OUTPUT = 'DONE'
END
